  "data": {
    "body": "Let $A$ be an $m \\times n$ matrix. Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n$$\n(i) If equation $A \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent for each $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m}$ then $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n.$ \n\n(ii) If equation $A \\mathbf{x}=0$ has only trivial solution, then $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n(iii) If $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ then rows of $A$ form a linearly dependent set.\n\n(iv) If $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $A$ is square matrix then $A$ is invertible.\n\n(v) If $ \\operatorname{rank}(A)=m$ and the linear transform $\\mathbf{x} \\mapsto A \\mathbf{x}$ is one-to-one then $A$ is invertible.\n",
    "solution": [
      3
    ],
